      "message": "fix(post): a milling operation is never posted on a lathe's work spindle\n\nA lathe post opens every section that states no C angle with the WORK\nspindle (G97 S M03). The stream names no operation family, so a milling\npass that stays on one meridian - a Face pass with an end mill along\nY = 0 - read to fanuc-lathe.cps and tormach-lathe.cps like a facing pass\nand posted the work spindle at the cutter's rpm with the cutter standing\nstill.\n\nThe program gate now decides it before a line is written, from what it\nalready holds (the operation's kind, its cached path, its work offset):\nthrough a turning dialect a section passes only as live-tool work (its\npath states C), a turning-family kind, or a Drill whose every cutting\nmove and cycle is on the spindle axis with the tool along +Z (how a\nlathe drills and taps on centre). Every other operation is refused by\nname. `app::lathe_voice::voice` is the one derivation; `at_post` is the\ndoor, called by the single-file, per-mount and per-operation posts, so\nthe GUI, the script verb and the MCP tool all take it. A mill post is\nuntouched.\n\nThe dialect is read from the script's own manifest (`capabilities`, the\nmask every shipped post already states) by `post::dialect::speaks_turning`;\n`post::dialect::states_live_tool` is the one \"does the path state C?\"\ntest, and the stream's PARAM LiveTool is written from it. No change to\nthe stream format, the CL spec or any post script; goldens unchanged.\n\nPinned by lathe_voice's unit table over every operation kind and by the\nlathe_work_spindle suite (both reproductions, every post entry point).\n\nFixes #1190\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
